Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:17:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 301/350] Assembly: a revolute joint can be driven by its angle
 (AngleDriven)

There was no proper way to turn a crank by an expression: the engine field
test drove it with a fixed joint whose Placement1 was an expression of a
rotation. A revolute joint now has AngleDriven; on, the second part is
turned to the joint's Angle about the joint's axis (Angle can be an
expression such as Params.theta). It is solved as a fixed joint whose first
placement is turned by the angle, so the walk of big steps and the check
that the joints hold see the angle too. In a simulation the motions turn
the joint as before.

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestAssemblySolve, -t TestAssemblyWorkbench

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
